From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:56:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mt6797-consys: remove the probe attributes on
 unload

The probe adds its region 19, firmware start and WLAN stop attributes
to the platform device by hand, and the unload left them there. After
an unload they pointed into freed module code: the next load could not
create them again (-EEXIST), and a write to region19_prepare crashed
in the unloaded module.

Remove them at the start of the unload, before it takes the locks
their writers take.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
index f4078e402..3ce82fdf4 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
@@ -2513,6 +2513,16 @@ static void mt6797_consys_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	int stop = -ENODEV, off = 0, ret;
 
+	/* The probe's files first: their writers take the locks below. */
+	device_remove_bin_file(dev, &bin_attr_region19_snapshot);
+	device_remove_file(dev, &dev_attr_region19_prepare);
+	device_remove_file(dev, &dev_attr_wmt_versions);
+	device_remove_file(dev, &dev_attr_wmt_negotiate);
+	device_remove_file(dev, &dev_attr_wmt_default_query);
+	device_remove_file(dev, &dev_attr_firmware_start_after_wmt);
+#if IS_MODULE(CONFIG_MT6797_MAC80211)
+	device_remove_file(dev, &dev_attr_wlan_stop);
+#endif
 	mutex_lock(&mt6797_consys_lock);
 #if IS_MODULE(CONFIG_MT6797_MAC80211)
 	mutex_lock(&mt6797_consys_wlan_lock);
-- 
